[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one parser bug, one fix queued. The reports in it
say otherwise. They hold three problems, and the queued parser fix closes only the first.

<Callout kind="warn">
Shipping the parser fix will not end #4471. Booking-v3 form bookings and the one-day moves keep
coming in until their own fixes ship.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

- **parser** — the shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants write the day
  first, so 7 April comes out as 4 July.
- **hint** — the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field and then reads the
  date day first. People do what the hint says, so their date flips. The parser fix does not
  touch this form.
- **shift** — some dates did not flip. They moved one day earlier, and people in different
  places saw different days for the same meeting. That is a time zone bug.

## Why one ticket hid three

- We merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). All three
  problems produce the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong"), so the
  subject cannot tell them apart.
- Intake tags come from the reporter's browser, not the tenant. Many reports carry the wrong
  tag, so the tags cannot tell them apart either.
- The kb's own table below found the hint bug and the one-day moves, then marked the first
  "no ticket of its own" and put the second in a footnote under `parser`.

## What the kb showed before this page

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What to do

1. Keep #4471 for the parser fix only.
2. Track the form hint and the one-day moves in their own tickets (linked in the table above).
3. Write a new decision record to replace 0001: merge on cause (tenant locale, booking form,
   channel), not on subject.

